# Mac + iPhone Universal

Dog Companion ships as **one codebase** for **iPhone** and **MacBook (Mac Catalyst)**. Every UI, feature, and bug fix must work on both — not just the platform you are testing on.

## Project setup

- `SUPPORTS_MACCATALYST = YES` in Xcode target — do not remove
- Mac destination: **My Mac (Mac Catalyst)**
- iOS destination: iPhone / Simulator
- Shared minimum: iOS 17 / macOS 14 (Catalyst)

## Required patterns

### Images

- Use `PlatformImage` (typealias for `UIImage` on Catalyst/iOS), never raw `UIImage` in Views
- Load with `PlatformImage.from(data:)`
- Display with `Image(platformImage:)`

### Platform checks

- Use `PlatformCapabilities.isMac` for copy/layout differences
- Use `PlatformCapabilities.isCameraAvailable` before showing camera UI
- Wrap camera / `UIImagePickerController` in `#if !targetEnvironment(macCatalyst)`

### UI layout

- Prefer `GeometryReader` and relative sizing (`geo.size.height * 0.28`) over fixed heights that only fit iPhone
- Full-screen scenes use `.ignoresSafeArea()` on background only; keep controls in safe area with padding
- Mac: `DogCompanionApp` uses `.defaultSize(width: 420, height: 780)` — new screens should look good in this window and on iPhone full screen
- Avoid `NavigationStack` large titles if they waste space on Mac; floating overlays (like HomeView top bar) are preferred for the focus room

### APIs

| API | iPhone | Mac Catalyst | Pattern |
|-----|--------|--------------|---------|
| PhotosPicker | ✅ | ✅ | Use for all photo picking |
| Camera | ✅ | ❌ | Guard with `#if !targetEnvironment(macCatalyst)` |
| Vision matting | ✅ | ✅ | Simulator needs CPU fallback (already in MattingService) |
| SwiftData | ✅ | ✅ | No platform guard needed |

### Do not

- Add iOS-only frameworks without Catalyst guards (HealthKit widgets, etc.)
- Hardcode "拍照" as the only photo entry on Mac
- Break Mac Catalyst build to fix iPhone-only issues — fix both

## Before finishing any task

1. Mentally verify the change on **iPhone** (portrait) and **Mac Catalyst** (resizable window)
2. If you added UIKit usage, confirm Catalyst compiles
3. If you added a new View file, add it to `project.pbxproj`
4. Commit and push (see `auto-push-github` rule)

## Key files

- `Utilities/PlatformImage.swift` — image type + `PlatformCapabilities`
- `Views/Components/SharedComponents.swift` — camera picker (iOS only)
- `Views/Creation/PhotoPickerView.swift` — platform-aware photo entry
